    "body": "## Current scope and sequence\nThe owner terminated Perf-01 and authorized DB-Scope-01 on Linux x64: retain the PostgreSQL/SQLite strongly typed Fluent ORM, Rust SeaQuery/SQLx and Native AOT; remove owned HTTP/gRPC/MCP and unrelated engine/demo products; verify, review, merge, then stop.\n\nThis Plan PR was established first at `b56ef7a6d4fc8c38cf8da04d555f30bae4e0693a`, before current Design and product edits. Old NativeWeave#19 and Plan#23 are closed unmerged. Old accessible-host task workspaces/processes/artifacts were cleared, with the inaccessible-host limitation recorded. Unrelated Dependabot PR3/4/7 are untouched.\n\n## What this PR records\n- Current scope, retain/remove dependency audit, seven ordered execution phases and source-bound acceptance entry.\n- Database Host and every implemented database capability remain in scope; applications choose their own standard HTTP/gRPC server.\n- Cargo/.NET/package/native/CI/docs pruning plus required fixture repairs, with every source-review and failure identity preserved.\n- Actual final CI workspaces, real PostgreSQL/SQLite regressions, outside-source PackageReference typed Fluent/DTO JIT/AOT consumers, package/output/loaded-native closure, genuine no-Rust SDK and runtime-only transfer evidence.\n- Independent technical review disclosures, exact artifact/source hashes, and normal PR/head/main-CI closeout.\n- Original 114 packets/three legacy graphs, historical source-driven baseline, accepted bindings and delivery history remain unchanged. Historical gates run against their immutable original inputs.\n\n## Actual results already recorded\n[Final candidate acceptance](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/c0068e00d67ee04d79d0d14785eb5aa81075b5d6/ledger/evidence/batches/DB-Scope-01/results/linux-acceptance-summary.md) binds product head `7255040b9501a1898d008c793f9b1777d8394d65`, tree `5f5d74ec7cfa502a4f8d119bb89e2e2776d4b65b`, to successful [CI44919645468](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/actions/runs/44919645468).\n\nAll56 database regression gates and86 Rust tests passed. PostgreSQL and SQLite ordinary PackageReference JIT/AOT consumption passed with typed DTO/data checks and exact loaded library identities. Twelve candidate packages, two provider native leaves, four lifecycle/business rows,32 finite faults,14 release/recovery cases,24 refusal guards in each ordinary/pristine consumer flow, and four runtime-only transfers passed. The unchanged semantic validator passed2,959 predicates; independent reviewers checked actual authenticated artifacts and source/log hashes. All original warnings and evidence limitations remain disclosed.\n\nTwelve of fourteen claims now pass. The global three-repository PR and merged-main CI claims remain pending, overall `in_progress`.\n\n## Delivery state\n- Design [PR14](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave-Design/pull/14) merged as `8298dc4128b745cf1809bad0c3cf02c45eb7f522`; both exact main checks passed and the merged tree equals the tested tree.\n- Product [PR20](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/pull/20) merged normally as `465cd0f90e6af05ec50eb581156240377cf0825b`; merged tree equals tested C10. Its complete [main CI44924918463](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/actions/runs/44924918463) passed. All required jobs/steps succeeded; Dependency review has its unchanged PR-only skip. Exact main run/job metadata and the source-bound receipt are now committed.\n- Both source repositories are delivered with successful main CI. This Plan delivery PR now awaits final integration review and exact-head checks for `c0068e00d67ee04d79d0d14785eb5aa81075b5d6` (tree `2b63ba34e3498ad688efd05a08844ff9b3c1de14`). After its normal merge/main CI is actually observed, the authorized evidence-only followup records the delivered snapshot as accepted and checks its own CI separately. No future or self-referential CI claim.\n\n[Handoff](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/DB-Scope-01-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/DB-Scope-01/handoff-linux.md) and [acceptance](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/DB-Scope-01-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/DB-Scope-01/acceptance.json) are the resume entry. Performance optimization, 30-minute load, new ORM features, new hosting wrappers, Windows validation and public package release remain deferred. No protections/licenses/required checks or approval identities were changed.",
